# Narrow path exemptions for leakscan. One glob per line, root-relative.
# This is NOT a blanket opt-out — every entry states why, and anything not
# listed here is scanned. Prefer an inline `leakscan:allow:` marker on the
# flagged line; use this file only for whole paths that are never published.

# setuptools build output, regenerated by `pip install -e .` and already in
# .gitignore, so it is never committed and never publishes. It merely restates
# the author byline from pyproject.toml, which carries its own inline marker.
src/*.egg-info/
